WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.627 --> 00:00:03.712
You guys ready?

00:00:09.134 --> 00:00:11.428
We're all hopping on different 
modes of transportation

00:00:11.428 --> 00:00:13.680
to explain the design choices 
behind the ways we travel.

00:00:13.972 --> 00:00:16.391
I'm so excited.

00:00:16.391 --> 00:00:17.559
Maybe this was a mistake.

00:00:23.023 --> 00:00:25.275
We can now build cruise ships 
that are as long

00:00:25.275 --> 00:00:27.902
as the Empire State Building is tall.

00:00:27.902 --> 00:00:29.112
How do they do that?

00:00:29.112 --> 00:00:31.156
You've arrived at LaGuardia Airport.

00:00:31.197 --> 00:00:33.116
Why does it feel like 
I'm getting less legroom

00:00:33.116 --> 00:00:34.659
on planes than I used to?

00:00:34.659 --> 00:00:36.161
The US used to have the biggest

00:00:36.161 --> 00:00:38.580
and most well-funded 
rail network in the world.

00:00:38.788 --> 00:00:39.873
What the heck happened?

00:00:39.873 --> 00:00:41.082
To find out the answer to that

00:00:41.082 --> 00:00:43.209
I’m going to take the Amtrak 
from here in Los Angeles

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:44.794
all the way to New York City.

00:00:44.794 --> 00:00:46.755
Oh! There’s an RV. 

00:00:46.755 --> 00:00:50.800
Why does every RV I see have 
the same swishes and swoops?

00:00:51.092 --> 00:00:54.012
I'm going to the RV capital of the world 
to find out.

00:00:54.345 --> 00:00:56.347
I just did a crazy turnaround

00:00:56.347 --> 00:00:58.433
because I just saw the coolest looking RV.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:01.269
So I'm going on a little 
East Coast road trip...

00:01:01.561 --> 00:01:04.898
and I'm 99% sure that 
most of the cars...

00:01:05.231 --> 00:01:08.568
are going to be bigger than mine.

00:01:12.322 --> 00:01:14.407
It's a 70 hour journey.

00:01:14.824 --> 00:01:16.367
I guess I better get started.

